From b45f79e47cff2a7a9fc4fa12281097d4f2f9a38b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:14:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Port RC-Cockpit's SPI display driver and software renderer to
 pico-sdk

Adds a new cockpit/ module to the project build: a bare pico-sdk SPI0
driver for the two ST7735 panels (display.c/.h, new code - the
original Arduino sketch had this inline in its .ino), plus near
verbatim ports of the pure software renderer that only ever touches
the shared backFB framebuffer (pfd.c/.h, map.c/.h, bootscreen.c/.h).

display.c's init sequence, panel geometry/offsets, SPI speeds, and
the panelColor() byte-order trick in pfd.h are all taken from a
previously flashed, working RP2350 build of this same cockpit code
(a 4-display variant), not re-derived from scratch - only the pin
numbers differ here (CS1/CS2 instead of CS1..CS4) to match the
Core2350B's 2-display layout.

map_bitmap.h is the original map_128x128_final.h with PROGMEM
stripped and an include guard added (RP2350 has a single unified
address space, so there's no separate flash-read path to keep);
the pixel data itself is byte-for-byte unchanged.

Not wired into main.c yet - that, plus the servo and IMU ports, are
still to come. This only adds the module and gets it building
cleanly alongside the existing MSRC/FreeRTOS tree.
